! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F209E "TEST FORCED ZERO
! RESULT", sub-tests E5-E8 (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.108,
! octal 015727.40-015765.00, where F209E9 begins).
!
! The same forced zero as E1-E4, reached from the other direction.
! E1-E4 subtracted a larger positive operand; E5-E8 ADD a negative one:
!
!   FPK38 = 0031052525252525252520
!   FPK43 = 0031125252525252525250
!
! FPK43 is FPK37 with its sign bit set -- same exponent 0031, same
! magnitude, negative. So D+MG(U) FPK43 adds a negative operand of
! larger magnitude to the accumulator's magnitude, the sum comes out
! negative, and p.95's forced zero applies. E1-E4 got there through
! D-MG on a positive operand; these get there through D+MG on a
! negative one, which is the arm of the sign-modifier decode that
! E1-E4 never touch.
!
!   E5  MS+1, ACS+N+A+0    DL(U)  FPK38 + D+MG(U)  FPK43   sign 0
!   E6  MS+N+A+1, ACS+0    DL(U)  FPK38 + D-MGA(U) FPK43   sign 0
!   E7  MS+ACS+1, N+A+0    DLN(U) FPK38 + D+MG(U)  FPK43   sign 1
!   E8  MS+ACS+N+A+1       DLN(U) FPK38 + D-MGA(U) FPK43   sign 1
!
! E6 and E8 are worth reading twice: D-MGA applies A first (forcing
! FPK43 positive) and then the minus (making it negative again), so
! they land on the same arithmetic as E5 and E7 by a different route
! through strip_fp_sign. That double inversion is what they check.
!
! As in E1-E4 the two CT0110 tests are 48 bits at offsets 20 and 68,
! covering IBM 12-107 -- the fraction only. The exponent at IBM 0-11
! is never compared here either, and the operand exponents are equal,
! so this block cannot settle the standing exponent question.
!
! E5 has no leading B,$+.32: it begins immediately after E4's last
! branch, at 015727.40.
!
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool p.176. PASS sits at 015765.00, where F209E9 begins.
!
! Instructions: B, DL(U), DLN(U), D+MG(U), D-MGA(U), CT0110, SIC, BB,
! BZB and BRGZ.
! verify_fp_arith_f209e5_8_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: all four passed on the first run, and an injection confirms
! the D-MGA claim above rather than leaving it as reasoning. Dropping
! the abs bit from strip_fp_sign's D-MGA rule -- returning
! ("D+MG", 0, 1) instead of ("D+MG", 1, 1), so the minus is applied
! without the preceding absolute -- halts E6 with SIC storing
! 015744.00, the address right after its high-order fraction question.
!
! The discrimination is exact, and worth stating because two other
! blocks use D-MGA and neither can see it:
!
!   F209E1-E4 stays green because its D-MGA operand is FPK37, which is
!   already POSITIVE -- abs is a no-op there, so both spellings give
!   the same operand. Only E5-E8's negative FPK43 tells them apart.
!
!   F209E9 stays green because it asks only about LS. Without the abs,
!   the operand comes out positive, the sum is positive and nonzero,
!   so there is no forced zero and no zero result fraction -- LS is
!   off either way, which is what E9 demands.
!
! So E6 (and E8, which is the same arithmetic with the accumulator
! negative) is the only place in the suite where the A-then-minus
! ordering is observable at all.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --
        SLC, (8)022005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
        SLC, (8)022053.0
FPK38   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031052525252525252520
        SLC, (8)022060.0
FPK43   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031125252525252525250

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)15727.40
ENTRY   DL(U), FPK38                       ! F209E5: MS+1, ACS+N+A+0
        D+MG(U), FPK43
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK0+.12, 20        ! test low order result fraction = 0
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK0+.12, 68        ! test high order result fraction = 0
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BZB, 10.4, $+2.0                   ! test sign bit = 0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        B, $+.32                           ! F209E6: MS+N+A+1, ACS+0
        DL(U), FPK38
        D-MGA(U), FPK43
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK0+.12, 20
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK0+.12, 68
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BZB, 10.4, $+2.0                   ! test sign bit = 0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        B, $+.32                           ! F209E7: MS+ACS+1, N+A+0
        DLN(U), FPK38
        D+MG(U), FPK43
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK0+.12, 20
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK0+.12, 68
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BB, 10.4, $+2.0                    ! test sign bit = 1
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        B, $+.32                           ! F209E8: MS+ACS+N+A+1
        DLN(U), FPK38
        D-MGA(U), FPK43
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK0+.12, 20
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK0+.12, 68
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BB, 10.4, $+2.0                    ! test sign bit = 1
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                             ! 015765.00: where F209E9 begins
        END, ENTRY
